Found during k126 (worker). With a source "path", a/Foo and b/foo are two catalog items but install into one directory on a case-insensitive file system. The standard layout cannot produce this inside one source (one skills/ directory); "path" can. Decide: treat names equal ignoring case as the k126 duplicate-name item error, on every platform so a lock stays portable (Windows port rule: same files and lock on Linux and Windows).

2026-10-15 03:28 Started (worker): decision as accepted – names equal ignoring case are the k126 duplicate-name item error on every platform. Each spelling stays its own catalog item (engine and commands match names exactly, so a config naming either one gets the error instead of 'not found'), each carrying one error naming every directory of the group.

2026-10-15 03:33 Also found (not in scope, for this board): the case collision is not path-only. The default scan on a case-sensitive FS offers skills/Foo beside skills/foo (one skills/ dir can hold both on Linux), agents/Foo.md beside agents/foo.md, and the same across plugin.json and .claude/ (those dedupe by exact name). Two different sources/scopes installing Foo and foo also land in one directory on macOS/Windows. Folding is String#toLowerCase, not the FS's own table; NFC/NFD (APFS normalization) is not handled. A follow-up card could apply one case-folded name check catalog-wide or at install planning.

